{"name":"Wimbledon","hex":"#626d5b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Wimbledon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A suburban town and the principal business area in the borough of Merton, Greater London, England .","A minor city in Pierce Township, Barnes County, North Dakota, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wimbledon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wimbledon, London","blocks":[{"text":"Wimbledon is a suburb of southwest London, England, 7.0 miles (11.3 km) southwest of Charing Cross; it is the main commercial centre of the London Borough of Merton. Wimbledon had a population of 68,189 in 2011 which includes the electoral wards of Abbey, Wimbledon Town and Dundonald, Hillside, Wandle, Village, Raynes Park and Wimbledon Park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Wimbledon.jpg/330px-Wimbledon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wimbledon%2C_London"},{"title":"Wimbledon Championships","blocks":[{"text":"The Wimbledon Championships, commonly called Wimbledon, is a tennis tournament organised annually in Wimbledon, London, by the All England Lawn Tennis and Croquet Club in collaboration with the Lawn Tennis Association. It is chronologically the third of the four Grand Slam tennis events each year, held after the Australian Open and the French Open and before the US Open. It is the oldest tennis tournament in the world and is widely regarded as the most prestigious."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b9/Wimbledon.svg/330px-Wimbledon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wimbledon_Championships"},{"title":"Wimbledon (constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"Wimbledon is a constituency in Greater London represented in the House of Commons of the UK Parliament. Since 2024, the seat has been held by Paul Kohler of the Liberal Democrats."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Wimbledon_2023_Constituency.svg/330px-Wimbledon_2023_Constituency.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wimbledon_(constituency)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/West_end_of_Caesar%27s_Camp%2C_Wimbledon_Common._-_geograph.org.uk_-_20689.jpg/500px-West_end_of_Caesar%27s_Camp%2C_Wimbledon_Common._-_geograph.org.uk_-_20689.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/West_end_of_Caesar%27s_Camp%2C_Wimbledon_Common._-_geograph.org.uk_-_20689.jpg/500px-West_end_of_Caesar%27s_Camp%2C_Wimbledon_Common._-_geograph.org.uk_-_20689.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Remains of the ditch between the two main ramparts of the Iron Age hill fort","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWest_end_of_Caesar's_Camp%2C_Wimbledon_Common._-_geograph.org.uk_-_20689.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Stmaryswimbledonsw19.jpg/500px-Stmaryswimbledonsw19.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Stmaryswimbledonsw19.jpg/1280px-Stmaryswimbledonsw19.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Stmaryswimbledonsw19.jpg/500px-Stmaryswimbledonsw19.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"St Mary's Church","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStmaryswimbledonsw19.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/ISH_Wimbledon3.jpg/500px-ISH_Wimbledon3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thum